{
  "$schema": "../schema.json",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "country-cm",
  "kind": "country",
  "country": "CM",
  "name": "Cameroon",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "verification": "draft",
  "notes": [
    "No Cameroonian statute or gazette was reachable for the public holidays: every holiday comes from a secondary source (Wikipedia) and is a draft. The statute that sets them was not found.",
    "Korite and Tabaski depend on the moon and are declared each year; no declaration was fetched, so none is listed and a year has none until its declaration is added.",
    "A holiday that falls on a Sunday is kept on its own day: no rule of observance was confirmed.",
    "The 10 regions and their ISO 3166-2 codes are read from a secondary copy of the ISO table, not from the official gazette. The division, the second level, is free text and no division list is bundled.",
    "No identifier format was found in a fetched source: every scheme is free text.",
    "The one statutory return is read from a row of the Directorate General of Taxes' fiscal calendar that concerns road transporters (VS/IRPP + IS + TVA, a monthly declaration and payment within 15 days of the month); whether it applies unchanged to a school's payroll withholding is unconfirmed.",
    "The pack covers the Francophone subsystem; the Anglophone subsystem (GCE) is a separate programme and not modelled by a country pack."
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "iso-3166-2-cm",
      "title": "ISO 3166-2:CM: subdivision codes of Cameroon (secondary copy of the ISO table)",
      "publisher": "Wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-2:CM",
      "accessed": "2026-10-27"
    },
    {
      "id": "holidays-cm",
